Loglan      bibliography      The founding document for the Loglan Project is      Loglan 1: A Logical Language      by James Cooke Brown (4th ed. 1989, The Loglan Institute, Gainesville, Florida, U.S.A.). The language in that book is not Lojban. It is the sibling language whose grammatical design Lojban shares (see
). The Loglan Institute continues to maintain and develop it, and it makes current materials available at
loglan.org.
